<h3 id="improved-explain-output" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Improved EXPLAIN output</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#improved-explain-output" aria-label="Link to Improved EXPLAIN output"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>Query optimization becomes easier in Postgres 18 thanks to the expanded EXPLAIN ANALYZE output. <a href="https://neon.com/postgresql/postgresql-18/enhanced-explain">Buffer usage is now included by default</a>, eliminating the need to add BUFFERS manually, and new metrics show the number of index lookups performed. In verbose mode, additional details such as CPU usage and WAL writes are also included.</p>
