<h3 id="uuidv7-support" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>UUIDv7 support</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#uuidv7-support" aria-label="Link to UUIDv7 support"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>Postgres 18 introduces <a href="https://neon.com/postgresql/postgresql-18/uuidv7-support">native support for UUIDv7</a>, a new RFC-standardized format that embeds a timestamp in the UUID. Unlike the random distribution of UUIDv4, UUIDv7 values are naturally ordered, which improves B-tree index performance and cache efficiency, which can be seen in better update and insert performance.</p>
