<p>The <code>RETURNING</code> clause has also been expanded in Postgres 18 to make <a href="https://neon.com/postgresql/postgresql-18/enhanced-returning">both old and new row values available in a single statement.</a> This allows developers to capture before-and-after values during INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, or MERGE operations without triggers or additional queries.</p>
